WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.049
Speaker 1: We've talked now for a while about
how if the American Right is really harping

00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:13.299
on the left is doing this, we should really
be considering whether it is they themselves

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:14.299
that are doing it.

00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:15.469
This is called projection.

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:19.670
This is accusing others of doing that, which
you are doing.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:25.150
And when it comes to free speech and cancel
culture, the right has been making a living

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.780
in some cases, literally making a living when
it comes to some of these right wing media

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.830
outlets by saying the left wants to cancel
anybody they don't agree with and the left

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.970
wants to take away your free speech.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:44.360
We have a fascinating but disturbing new report
about the book ban, effort and book ban.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.289
Efforts have hit their highest level in at
least 20 years, and it is not the left that

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:50.320
is doing it.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.260
It is the right that is trying to do it.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.649
So we are going to look at this report from
the American Library Association.

00:00:56.649 --> 00:00:58.839
It was released earlier this week.

00:00:58.839 --> 00:01:07.000
The report found over 700 challenges to library,
school and university materials in 2021.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.850
This is the most since at least 2000.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:15.260
The ALA has only been tracking such efforts
since the year 2000, so we can say it's been

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.120
at least 20 years, but maybe more.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:25.570
Axios goes on to say book bands have risen
substantially over the past year as conservative

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:32.820
groups have challenged public school libraries
and successfully purged books from those libraries,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:39.660
generally about LGBTQ issues, which they like
to frame as, you know, inappropriate gender

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:45.830
and sexuality indoctrination and books about
people of color, which they often like to

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:51.850
frame as teaching white people to feel bad
or critical race theory, or whatever the case

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.140
may be.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:58.080
Now there's a bunch of different important
elements to this that we need to talk about.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.250
First is again, I'm going to say this a bunch
of times.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.000
This is right wingers.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.800
This is right wingers doing this.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:09.690
They say they are for free speech, but they
want to ban or challenge books.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:16.230
They say they are against canceling, but they
want to cancel authors of books or cancel

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:22.079
a teacher's right or ability to say, Here's
the material I want to teach with, and here's

00:02:22.079 --> 00:02:23.549
how I'm going to teach with it.

00:02:23.549 --> 00:02:27.980
They are the ones who are the experts in education,
but it is random people who say, No, no, no,

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.819
no, you shouldn't be allowed to do that.

00:02:29.819 --> 00:02:33.530
Now that is the projection and hypocrisy piece.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:37.739
Oftentimes, you know, the people most loudly
talking about free speech are the ones trying

00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:39.299
to limit it.

00:02:39.299 --> 00:02:40.739
When is it OK to ban books?

00:02:40.739 --> 00:02:44.079
Is it ever OK to ban books in this?

00:02:44.079 --> 00:02:46.750
There is an important and serious conversation
to have.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.750
In other words.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:53.000
Are we saying block certain books from being
published?

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.189
Basically never.

00:02:54.189 --> 00:02:58.569
There is essentially never.

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:02.269
We might be able to come up with a couple
of examples of when we are saying it should

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:06.659
be against the law for a publisher to even
publish certain books.

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:11.310
Are we saying don't have certain books in
certain libraries?

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.879
OK, well, so let's now imagine.

00:03:13.879 --> 00:03:17.370
Should there be pornography in an elementary
school library up?

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:18.370
No.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:24.760
Should there be books that are instruction
manuals on how to make bombs in elementary

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.040
school libraries?

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.580
Probably not.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.629
But here we're already talking about age restrictions.

00:03:30.629 --> 00:03:33.239
That's very different than a ban.

00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:37.349
And then there's the question of, well, what
about as part of class curriculum?

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:43.170
Should eight year olds have certain materials
as part of their class curriculum?

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:47.510
And they're my idea is similar to my view
on responsible platforming.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:50.139
Sometimes I'll interview a lunatic extremist.

00:03:50.139 --> 00:03:52.810
We used to interview the people from that
Westboro Baptist Church, and we would get

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:57.790
emails sometimes from people saying, you shouldn't
have these people on because your platforming

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:58.790
them.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:01.590
And my response was responsible.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:07.370
Platforming means I've determined the views
are worth exposing.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:12.319
And I feel equipped to make it clear that
the views are disgusting.

00:04:12.319 --> 00:04:15.310
And that was the difference between some of
the interviews I would do and some of the

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.160
ones that you would see elsewhere.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.860
Similarly, I would apply the same kind of
test when it comes to school curriculum.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:30.060
I understand saying, you know, we don't want
teachers teaching Hitler's Mein Kampf unless

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:35.370
they are equipped to teach it correctly and
to teach it in a way that makes it abundantly

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:42.530
clear that these are the disgusting views
of a xenophobic, authoritarian maniac who

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.040
had six million Jews killed.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.880
It starts to get more complicated.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.470
There's not one answer.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.450
But the point here is.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.530
We are not saying ban the book.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:55.880
We are not saying burn the book.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:05:01.570
And I remember in my high school history of
film class, there were discussions about what

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:05.640
movies is it OK for 14 year olds to watch?

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:13.040
What level of gratuitous violence and sexuality
is OK for the classroom doesn't mean, you

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.530
know, throw away.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:18.010
What would at the time were DVDs doesn't mean
don't allow parents to weigh.

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:21.100
But there were questions like what is appropriate
for 14 year olds to watch in school?

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.190
It's a fair question.

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:24.070
Is it too sexually explicit?

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:30.000
And then we get to the hypocritical aspect
of the book bands that they demand, and that

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.940
can't be ignored because they'll say, Oh,
this is too sexually explicit, but they're

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:39.100
OK with the sexuality that's in the Bible,
which is extreme and significant.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.180
They say this is too violent, but they're
OK with all of the violence in the Bible.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:46.910
They make exceptions there, so the hypocrisy
is a major component.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:52.480
There is a real conversation to be had here,
and in almost all cases, we shouldn't be banning

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:56.690
books, but we can't even have that conversation
with the right because they just want them

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:57.690
axed.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.950
They want to decide what teachers are allowed
to do.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:03.440
They want to decide what librarians are allowed
to have in the library, and it's a bad faith

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.570
conversation from the ground up.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.580
Let me know your thoughts.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.520
You can find me on Twitter at Packman and
let me know what you think

